{"type":"text","timestamp":1794251096576,"sessionID":"ses_e3e565f43ffeFYniwGyz6OhCbl","part":{"id":"prt_1c1b301e2001hrrYM93hsl8VVe","messageID":"msg_1c1b2d4e0001lp3BxvvRuudHQM","sessionID":"ses_e3e565f43ffeFYniwGyz6OhCbl","type":"text","text":"I've built the notes app: the Flask API, the React/TypeScript/Tailwind frontend and the SQLite storage in `./data`. The 4 backend tests pass, a run against a live gunicorn server worked, and `npm run build` succeeds with type checking. Two things are untested: there's no Docker here, so the image has never been built, and the browser download needed the network, so nobody has clicked through the UI yet.\n\n**Backend** (`backend/app.py`)\n- All the endpoints in the spec are in place, with the field names and status codes you listed, plus `GET /api/health`.\n- Login returns a random token. Only a hash of it is stored, and it expires after 30 days. A missing or invalid token gets 401.\n- Another user's note returns 404, the same as a note that doesn't exist. An unpublished note's public page is also 404.\n- Markdown is turned into HTML with markdown-it-py, and the result is cleaned with nh3. Raw HTML in a note is shown as text, and `javascript:` links are stripped.\n- I added a few endpoints you didn't ask for: `GET /api/auth/me`, `POST /api/auth/logout`, and `GET /api/public/notes/{id}`. The last one gives the public page the title and author.\n- Repeating a username returns 409, and bad input returns 400.\n\n**Frontend**\n- **Sign-in:** registration and sign-in forms, then a header showing the username and a sign-out button.\n- **Notes list:** most recently updated first, with a Published badge.\n- **Editor:** saves automatically about half a second after you stop typing. The preview next to it is fetched from `GET /api/notes/{id}/html` after each save, so it lags typing slightly rather than updating on every keystroke.\n- **Publishing:** the Published switch shows the public link with a Copy button.\n- **Public page:** `/p/{id}` shows the title, the author and the rendered note.\n\n**Other changes**\n- New dependencies: `markdown-it-py` and `nh3` for the backend, and Tailwind and TypeScript for the frontend. Both lock files are updated.\n- `npm run build` now runs the type check first.\n- I added backend tests in `backend/tests/`, run with `pytest backend/tests`, and a `.gitignore`.\n\nTo finish checking, run `docker build` and then open the app in a browser.","time":{"start":1794251096546,"end":1794251096552}}}
